yaml_takeover.description:
Entities of the YAML package (homeassistant_lg_therma_v_modbus) are still in Home Assistant, with their history. {count} of them have a counterpart here. Taking them over renames each to the integration's entity id, so its history and long-term statistics continue there, and removes the old entity. Nothing is deleted from the database.

{takeover_table}

⚠ The unit is spelled differently (e.g. U/min → rpm). The history continues; Home Assistant then asks once under *Developer tools → Statistics* to confirm the new unit. The values are the same.

Not taken over, left as they are:

{left_table}

① the integration scales the value differently · ② not a temperature · ③ different unit · ④ text instead of a number, or different texts · ⑤ a different entity type here (number, button) · ⑥ the YAML is still loaded: remove it and restart first · ⑦ the entity id is already taken
